Description: Reduce per-frame and per-repaint cost of the XDJ additions
 Pure cost reductions: no control, no config key and no observable behaviour
 changes. Every item below is work the earlier patches in this series
 introduced on a hot path, found while profiling why the console feels
 sluggish on a Pi 4.
 .
 1. Waveform bar markers (xdj-hardware.patch) ran three avoidable costs per
    waveform, per deck, per frame:
    - The downbeat X positions were collected into a function-local QVector
      that reallocated on every draw(). It is now a member, cleared and
      reused, matching why upstream keeps m_beats as a member.
    - Each downbeat issued two separate drawPolygon() rasterisations. All
      triangles now go into one reused QPainterPath filled with a single
      drawPath().
    - `it - firstMarker` was recomputed for every beat. mixxx::Beats'
      const_iterator is not guaranteed random-access, so operator- can
      degrade to an O(n) std::distance(), making the loop O(n^2) per frame.
      The offset is computed once before the loop and incremented.
    The allshader/QOpenGL renderer gets the same iterator fix plus a reserve()
    on its downbeat vertex buffer.
 .
 2. Key traffic light (library-ui.patch) invalidated the entire model --
    rowCount() x columnCount() -- through the sort/filter proxy on every deck
    play/pause and every master-deck track change, i.e. continuously during a
    mix, over rekordbox playlists that can run to thousands of rows. Only the
    Key column's background can change, so only that column is invalidated.
 .
 3. The same traffic light called KeyUtils::guessKeyFromText() -- a string
    parse -- once per Key cell per repaint, and roleValue() parsed the same
    string a second time for the displayed note name. Both now share a
    memoized text->ChromaticKey map on XdjMasterKeyTracker; a library has a
    few dozen distinct key strings at most.
 .
 4. The visible-rows zoom and the fixed column layout (library-ui.patch) both
    recomputed and re-applied their derived values from inside resizeEvent().
    setFont(), setMinimumSectionSize(), setDefaultSectionSize() and
    setColumnWidth() each relayout the header and repaint the viewport, and a
    resize that only changes width leaves every derived number identical.
    Both now early-out when nothing changed, with explicit invalidation where
    the guard cannot see the change (a new base font, a newly loaded model).
 .
 5. The controller reconnect watchdog (xdj-hardware.patch) ran a full PortMidi
    + HID enumeration every 5 s forever whenever a controller was enabled in
    the preferences but not plugged in -- a recurring hitch and constant
    background CPU for a device that may never return. The first three
    attempts stay at 5 s so replugging still reconnects promptly (the
    documented behaviour), then the interval doubles to a 60 s ceiling and
    resets as soon as everything enabled is open again.
Author: Pioneered fork
Forwarded: no

